'''Tholothians''' were a [[species]] of [[Sentience|sentient]] [[near-human]]s [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Tholoth]]. They could be distinguished from typical [[human]]s by their partial [[color]]ful skin pigmentation, their scaled craniums and fleshy white, blue, or red tendrils that sprouted from their skullcaps. [[Jedi Master]]s [[Adi Gallia]], [[Stass Allie]], [[Jedi Knight]] [[Indeera Stokes]], former [[Padawan]] [[Ty Yorrick]], and the [[Jedi Initiate|youngling]] [[Katooni]] were members of the species.

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:Katooni-TCWs5BR1.png|thumb|left|180px|Katooni, a female Tholothian youngling]]
Tholothians were a [[near-human]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]].<ref name="Unlimited Power" /> Largely similar to [[human]]s in appearance, their primary distinguishing characteristics were their scaled skullcaps that sprouted fleshy head-tendrils, and their partially [[color]]ful skin pigmentation,<ref name="TholothianDB" /> particularly around the [[eye]]s.<ref name="KatooniDB">{{Databank|katooni|Katooni}}</ref> The Tholothians' skullcaps could be gold, brown, white,<ref name="TholothianDB" /> red,<ref name="Dark Lord 4" /> or blue in color.<ref name="Star Wars 2020 1">[[Star Wars (2020) 1|''Star Wars'' (2020) 1]]</ref> Some Tholothians, such as [[D'urban Wen-Hurd]], possessed [[hair]] on their heads.<ref name="Brotherhood">[[Brotherhood (novel)|''Brotherhood'']]</ref> [[Gender|Male]] Tholothians could grow facial hair.<ref name="Halcyon Legacy 1">[[Halcyon Legacy 1|''Halcyon Legacy'' 1]]</ref> Their skin could be brown, tan<ref name="Episode I" /> or pale.<ref name="Dark Lord 4" /> It was possible for Tholothians to be [[Force-sensitive]].<ref name="AdiGalliaDB">{{Databank|adi-gallia|Adi Gallia}}</ref>

==Society and culture==
The [[Tholothian government]], which governed the species' [[homeworld]] of [[Tholoth]], was a [[democracy]] with an executive branch and a senate of legislators. The government banished heavy industry to other [[planet]]s in the [[Tholoth system]] to preserve the natural environment of Tholoth. The government also instituted policies to limit the flow of offworld visitors, and insisted that newcomers integrate in ways that minded Tholoth's ecology. Tholothian [[City|cities]] incorporated foreign architectural designs with distinct Tholothian twists.<ref name="Unlimited Power" />

Traditional [[Tholoth headdress]]es were worn by many Tholothians as part of their culture. The headdresses featured fabric bands along the edges in varied shapes and sizes which held the cap in place and covered the [[ear]]s, connected to an ornamental web of delicate chains and beads tracing along the often tessellated scales along the wearer's scalp.<ref name="Updated and Expanded">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref>

==History==
[[File:Tholothian_Mystic_UP_Audrey_Hotte.png|thumb|right|200px|A Tholothian mystic Force user given in to the [[dark side of the Force]].]]
Tholothians were native to [[Tholoth]], an [[Forest|arboreal]] planet located in the Tholoth [[Star system|system]] of [[the galaxy]]'s [[Colonies]] and [[The Slice|Slice]] regions. Establishing their own planetary government, the Tholothians joined the [[Galactic Republic]], the predominant [[Galaxy|galactic]] polity. However, when the Republic was [[Proclamation of the New Order|transformed]] into the [[Galactic Empire]] at the end of the [[Clone Wars]], the new totalitarian state occupied Tholoth, turning it into a [[prison]] for its residents while high-ranking Imperial officials built palatial estates for themselves in Tholoth's protected zones.<ref name="Unlimited Power" />

==Tholothians in the galaxy==
Several Tholothians were members of the [[The Force|Force-using]] [[Jedi Order]] during the [[Republic Era]]. During the [[High Republic Era]], [[Padawan]] [[Ty Yorrick|Tylera]] was part of the Order until she departed following a traumatic incident at the [[Yallow Shrine]],<ref name="MOTP 4">[[The High Republic Adventures — The Monster of Temple Peak 4|''The High Republic Adventures — The Monster of Temple Peak'' 4]]</ref> after which she became the [[mercenary]] Ty Yorrick.<ref name="Rising Storm">''[[The High Republic: The Rising Storm]]''</ref> During the final [[Standard decade|decades]] of the Republic's existence, [[Jedi Master]] [[Adi Gallia]] sat on the [[Jedi High Council]]<ref name="Adi DB">{{Databank|adi-gallia|Adi Gallia}}</ref> until her [[death]] during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Revival">{{TCW|Revival (episode)}}</ref> Other Tholothian [[Jedi]] who served during the period included [[Stass Allie]], Gallia's successor on the Council,<ref name="StassAllieDB">{{Databank|stass-allie|Stass Allie}}</ref> as well as the [[Jedi Initiate|youngling]] [[Katooni]],<ref name="KatooniDB" /> Padawan [[Nim Pianna]],<ref name="Master & Apprentice">''[[Master & Apprentice]]''</ref> and [[Jedi Knight]] [[D'urban Wen-Hurd]].<ref name="Brotherhood" />

